Use one of these, depending on context:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(void) {
    return 0;          // Normal success exit
}
```

Or explicitly:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);    // Normal termination; runs atexit handlers, flushes stdio
```

For an error:

```c
exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
```

If you need to end immediately without cleanup handlers or normal stdio flushing:

```c
#include <unistd.h>

_exit(1);
```

In most cases, `return 0;` from `main` is the cleanest move.
